WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:15.370
Unit 1 · How Computers Work · done!

3
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:20.810
Unit 2 · Thinking Like a Computer

4
00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:26.110
Chapter 1 · What Is an Algorithm?

5
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:32.860
Al · go · rithm. Sounds big, right?

6
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:40.560
You already do it every day!

7
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:47.230
Meet Robo, your robot helper

8
00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:54.220
"Robo, please get me some water!"

9
00:00:54.220 --> 00:01:00.490
Robo just stands there…

10
00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:06.580
Why didn't Robo move? Think!

11
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:19.470
Robo needs every step, told clearly

12
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:34.490
Glass → Filter → Fill → Bring it to me

13
00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:46.490
Clear steps → Robo gets it right!

14
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:52.130
That list is called an ALGORITHM

15
00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.970
A clear list of steps, in order, to get a job done

16
00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:11.840
Steps · In order · A job done

17
00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:18.780
Have you watched someone make chai?

18
00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:33.270
Boil water → Tea leaves → Milk & sugar → Pour

19
00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:40.840
A recipe is an algorithm!

20
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:52.890
Wrong order = no chai. Order matters!

21
00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:59.290
You follow an algorithm every morning!

22
00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:10.180
Brush · Bath · Uniform · Bag · Tiffin

23
00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:20.460
5 steps in order → ready for school!

24
00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:28.840
Robots follow exactly. They can't guess.

25
00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:40.190
"Help the plant" → Help it how?

26
00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:46.970
Clear: "Pour one cup of water on the soil"

27
00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:55.370
Good algorithms: Short · Clear · Complete

28
00:03:55.370 --> 00:04:04.430
Short: no extra steps (no chai dance!)

29
00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.580
Clear: each step says exactly what to do

30
00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:16.930
Complete: no missing steps

31
00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:21.700
Detective game: find the missing step!

32
00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:36.310
Take a glass → ??? → Drink the water

33
00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:44.930
Missing step: pour water into the glass!

34
00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:52.430
Uh-oh! The sandwich steps are mixed up

35
00:04:52.430 --> 00:05:07.740
Which step comes first?

36
00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:21.220
Bread → Jam → Top slice → Cut & enjoy

37
00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:27.940
Your turn: practice check

38
00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:38.780
Write 4 steps to water a plant, for Robo

39
00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:55.190
Can → Fill → Walk → Pour on the soil

40
00:05:55.190 --> 00:06:02.850
Algorithm = clear steps, in order

41
00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:07.720
Recipes & routines are algorithms

42
00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:13.290
Robots can't guess, so be clear

43
00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:16.790
Good = Short · Clear · Complete

44
00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:22.890
Chapter 1 done!

45
00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:29.690
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
